    "explanation": "Both sides' kept claims point the same way, and the record decides this case on the instruments.\n\nFor the rider: the driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02753, weight 1.0) shows the vehicle holding position at the pin, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, continuously from 13:39:22 to 13:47:11 — a qualifying in-geofence dwell of 469 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; trip EV-TRIP-02753, weight 1.0). The trip record shows the driver's 'arrived' event at 13:39:22, the wait timer starting at 13:39:24, and the driver cancelling at 13:47:15 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 are therefore met and the SGD 4.50 no-show fee charged on EV-FARE-02753 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, reconciling with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd = 4.50, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect) stands. Your claim that 'the driver admitted fault' is not supported by the chat (EV-CHAT-02753): the only driver message is 'hi im at the pickup point' at 13:39:47, and your own message at 13:41:22 is a text purporting to be a system notice — it is not an admission by the driver and it has no effect on this ruling. Your own device track places you 884–892 m from the pickup pin throughout the waiting window with no fix inside the 100 m rider presence radius, so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you (limb (a) fails on the message content and limb (c) is affirmatively failed on your own admissible fixes; the driver-side submission that limb (b) would fail is not the reason — limb (b) would in fact be met, since the driver never replied within 120 s of your message and no in-app call is recorded, but the clause needs all three limbs). POL-NS-03 does not apply (the driver's stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius, not a wrong-entrance case, and the 400 m test is not reached). POL-NS-05 does not displace the fee: at the arrival marker the trace places the driver at the pin and stationary, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or above. POL-NS-06 does not displace it: there is no waiting-period shortfall, 469 s against a 180 s minimum.\n\nFor the driver: POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 fixes your payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee, being SGD 3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip — no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/63 = 0.016 (below 0.08) — so compensation is paid. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60; the contested charge itself is not refunded.\n\nNo escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is met: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 for both parties and no_show_disputes_30d is 1; the anti-farming check does not trip; and no deciding fact rests on evidence impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). EV-ADVIS-02753-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no deciding fact — POL-NS-06(i) cannot be run on it and is not needed, because the single 469-second run already exceeds the minimum. The driver's counterparty statement ('I waited the full period at the pin') carries no weight multiplier and adds nothing to the cap, which is 1.0, every deciding artifact (EV-GPS-02753, EV-TRIP-02753, EV-FARE-02753, EV-DPROF-02753) being at weight 1.0. The two claims about the missing advisory were discarded by the referee for citing an impaired artifact without naming its issue code (MISSING_ARTIFACT); they are recorded in the audit and not reinstated. No clause produces a referral on these facts. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
